What this fork changed (summary; see audit/SECURITY-AUDIT.md and
audit/hardening.patch for the complete diff):

  - Replaced shell-based provisioning with a fail-closed, Python
    standard-library-only single-intent launcher (a1grab.py).
  - Removed the upstream DRY_RUN launch defect, unbounded retries, and the
    absence of an idempotency journal / opc-retry-token.
  - Reworked configuration parsing to treat config as inert data (no
    source/eval), added a hard-coded Tokyo / A1 / 2 OCPU / 12 GB / 50 GB target.
  - Removed the generic notification path and third-party webhook/token reads.
  - Replaced the system service template with a read-only user unit.
  - Added full-tenant verification, billing/usage gating, local locking,
    persistent state, and an offline Mock-OCI test suite.

Binary dependencies under .audit-tools/ are intentionally NOT included in this
repository. See README (source/license notice) and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md
(section 2) for how to obtain and verify them via audit/dependency-manifest.json.

No OCI credentials, API keys, private keys, tenancy identifiers, or real
account configuration are included in this repository.

This fork is maintained independently. Please report issues to this repository,
not to the upstream author.
